  "sa": "षष्ठोऽनुवाकः",
  "en": "The gods, each with Indra"
 },
 "summary": "Twenty deities and regions are named, and after each comes Indra: Agni and Indra, Soma and Indra, through the Maruts, the All-gods, earth, atmosphere and sky, the quarters and the ‘head’, to Prajāpati. Sāyaṇa explains the pairing: Indra has an equal share with all of them, so he is recited with each deity in turn. The quarters are the four directions beginning with the east, and the ‘head’ is the upward direction, named apart as the chief.",
